  "id": "latent-construct",
  "term": "latent construct",
  "definition": "A latent construct is an underlying psychological attribute or structure that is not observed directly but is inferred from measured indicators or items. Its latent form may be understood as categorical or dimensional, and that structure affects how the construct is defined, measured, and studied.",
